      "text": "Buildings in very cold climates, such as Alaska, are often made of ice. Renewable resources that help conserve energy are used as building materials. The inside of the building is designed so that as little cooling or heating as possible is needed. This type of architecture is named green architecture because it helps to keep the Earth green and healthy. Solar or wind energy is used whenever possible because it is renewable. How many buildings in your area can be called green?",
